WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.155
This video is about the rack where every one
of your cable paths begins: the TPU rack.

2
00:00:09.505 --> 00:00:17.085
We will cover what a TPU is, the two faces of
the rack, each unit from top to bottom, which

3
00:00:17.085 --> 00:00:21.750
parts are yours, and the six cable groups that
leave it.

4
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.420
TPU stands for Tensor Processing Unit.

5
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:37.189
It is a computer chip designed for the kind of
math that artificial intelligence uses.

6
00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:44.086
The guide calls the rack that holds these
computers a TPU rack.

7
00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:50.489
Sometimes it just says TPU, as in TPU one to
seventy-two.

8
00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:55.295
The drawings call it an Ironwood TPU rack.

9
00:00:56.645 --> 00:01:03.792
From public sources, not the guide: Ironwood
is Google's seventh-generation TPU.

10
00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:11.136
A rack holds sixty-four chips, it is liquid
cooled, and racks connect to each other

11
00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:13.758
through optical circuit switches.

12
00:01:14.508 --> 00:01:17.751
That is why you install OCS cables.

13
00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:26.701
A TPU rack has two faces, side A and side B.

14
00:01:27.451 --> 00:01:30.181
Parts outlined in black are yours.

15
00:01:30.931 --> 00:01:34.878
Grey parts are pre-installed, and you leave
them alone.

16
00:01:36.878 --> 00:01:40.334
At the top of each side are three rectifiers.

17
00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:46.161
They turn incoming power into the DC power the
rack uses.

18
00:01:46.911 --> 00:01:48.127
Not yours.

19
00:01:49.477 --> 00:01:53.317
Below them on side A is the top of rack
switch.

20
00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:57.971
On side B, the same space is a blank panel.

21
00:01:59.321 --> 00:02:04.036
The top of rack switch is the rack's door to
the data network.

22
00:02:04.786 --> 00:02:08.733
Your 144-fiber trunk plugs into it.

23
00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:14.361
Next is the TROSS unit, one on each side.

24
00:02:15.111 --> 00:02:16.988
The drawings say TROSS.

25
00:02:17.738 --> 00:02:24.223
The cutsheet calls them rmu1 on side A and
rmu2 on side B.

26
00:02:24.973 --> 00:02:26.979
Same box, two names.

27
00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:32.500
Below the TROSS is the OCS panel.

28
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.853
The cutsheet calls it pp1.

29
00:02:36.603 --> 00:02:43.024
Ports one to twelve are on side A, and
thirteen to twenty-four are on side B.

30
00:02:44.374 --> 00:02:51.573
The rest of the rack is machine trays, the AI
computers themselves, with batteries at the

31
00:02:51.573 --> 00:02:52.139
bottom.

32
00:02:52.889 --> 00:02:54.617
All pre-installed.

33
00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:56.967
Do not touch them.

34
00:03:01.117 --> 00:03:05.725
So on a TPU rack, you connect exactly four
things.

35
00:03:06.725 --> 00:03:08.645
The top of rack switch.

36
00:03:09.995 --> 00:03:14.582
The two TROSS units, rmu1 and rmu2.

37
00:03:15.932 --> 00:03:20.284
And the OCS panel, pp1, on both sides.

38
00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:29.072
Everything else, including the even ports on
the top of rack switch and the short internal

39
00:03:29.072 --> 00:03:30.807
cables, is not yours.

40
00:03:31.557 --> 00:03:36.421
Remember: if a cable never leaves the rack, it
is not yours.

41
00:03:40.571 --> 00:03:45.499
On the hall map, each TPU rack had six colored
stripes.

42
00:03:46.249 --> 00:03:48.511
Here is what they stand for.

43
00:03:49.911 --> 00:03:56.908
One 144-fiber trunk, from the top of rack
switch to the end of row rack.

44
00:03:58.258 --> 00:04:07.417
Three OCS cables: red, orange and yellow, from
the OCS panel to the three SPOCS racks of the

45
00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:07.815
pod.

46
00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:13.325
Two gig E copper runs, one from each TROSS
unit.

47
00:04:14.675 --> 00:04:21.563
And four more copper runs: the switch's
management and console ports, and the console

48
00:04:21.563 --> 00:04:23.507
port on each TROSS unit.

49
00:04:24.857 --> 00:04:32.495
The next lessons follow each of these groups,
starting with the 144-fiber trunk.

50
00:04:36.645 --> 00:04:43.591
In lesson six of the course, explore every
unit of the rack and practice finding the

51
00:04:43.591 --> 00:04:45.327
parts that are yours.

